# ROADMAP — Project Status, Release Pin & Active Sprint Backlog

File: openOODA/ROADMAP.oot
NORTHSTAR is the vision. SHIPPED is what exists. ROADMAP is the active execution plan and release pin.

## 1. Release Pin & Status

  Release: v0.199.0-alpha (Heading to v0.200.0-beta)
  Product tip (ooda): main
  Boards tip: main
  Std tip: main
  Beta is not the current release.

## 2. Compiler Health Metrics & Model

  Live check (this host): `oodac check oodac/main.oo` passes OK in about 150 seconds (178 modules).
  Memory model: `PURE_NO_ARC=0`. Memory is freed when the last reference drops.
  Native path: You do not need wasmtime, clang, or a special env file for the native C path.
  Std footprint: about 199 .oo files under `../ooda/std`. Org `std/` is not product.

## 3. Pure Rebuild Commands & Verification

  How to rebuild the compiler cleanly from `ooda/`:
    cd ../ooda
    export PURE_NO_ARC=0
    OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
    OODAC_BIN=./oodac/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
    ./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo
  PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 is opt-in only. It is not the official product path.

  CI honesty:
    `oodac check scripts/ci_product.oo` only typechecks those rails.
    It does not emit, gcc, or run them.
    Official rebuild is `bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`.
    Named emit+gcc+run proof is `scripts/ci_open_run.oo`.

## 4. Status Words

  done — works, proved on disk
  smoke — small check passes
  partial — part works
  residual — wanted in NORTHSTAR, not yet built
  open — active sprint task in current cycle

## 5. Open (This Cycle)

  From NORTHSTAR vs SHIPPED. Not a beta tag. Not ROADMAP section 6.
  Gemini owns org `std/`. Do not take that lane unless the owner names a file.
  This cycle's 13 rows are proved and marked done.

  [x] OPEN-1: `ooda test` runs `verify` / `assert_eq!` / `assert!` and fails closed. Not the same as `ooda run`.
  [x] OPEN-2: Check refuses unused `Result` (NORTHSTAR must-use). No discarded `expect_*` then PASSED.
  [x] OPEN-3: `ooda fix` and `ooda patch` write through `&FsWriteCap` / `write_file`. No host `printf` write.
  [x] OPEN-4: One more `ooda fix` class (missing import or parse/brace). Still ask unless `--yes`.
  [x] OPEN-5: Type floor for `Option` / exhaustive `match` / `?`. Compiler, not more library files.
  [x] OPEN-6: Official rebuild does not skip check (`PURE_SKIP_CHECK` is not the product path).
  [x] OPEN-7: A named CI set emits, gcc, and runs. `oodac check scripts/ci_product.oo` is not that proof.
  [x] OPEN-8: Product `oodac check --json-errors` is in-process. No capture `.sh`. Product CLI already converts.
  [x] OPEN-9: Product std is `ooda/std`. Org `std/` is not product until proved the same way.
  [x] OPEN-10: `cli/host_run.oo` under 256 lines (RULES 1.7).
  [x] OPEN-11: Tree `oodac` can emit the product CLI (same-file user calls). No older binary required.
  [x] OPEN-12: Check line/col is per source file after import. Not the expanded concat stream.
  [x] OPEN-13: `ooda.ebnf` matches what check accepts, and names what is residual.

## 6. Later / Residual Tracks (Not This Week's Sprint)

  These rows are wanted in NORTHSTAR. They are not the active sprint.
  Do not pick one unless the owner names the row.

### Track 1: Compiler & Code Generation Floor
  [ ] RTB-6: Pure .wasm binary bytecode emission (upgrade from .wat text to \0asm direct module).
  [ ] RTB-7: Self-host compiler check performance (<10s check & memory optimization under 250MiB).
  [ ] RTB-8: LLVM self-hosting expansion (struct matching & multi-module clang link parity).

### Track 2: Security, Sandboxing & OS Containment
  [ ] RTB-9: Linux Kernel Landlock sandboxing (filesystem path jails under &FsCap).
  [ ] RTB-10: POSIX heap rlimits & memory quotas (hard address-space ceilings under &MemCap).
  [ ] RTB-11: Fine-grained struct field secret taint tracking (allow clean fields, reject secret sinks).

### Track 3: Developer Ecosystem & Tooling Floor
  [ ] RTB-12: Pure self-hosted language server (ooda lsp native JSON-RPC binary replacing JS bridge).
  [ ] RTB-13: Multi-error in-place code fixer (ooda fix auto-patching E_CAP, missing imports & types).
  [ ] RTB-14: Package registry & cryptographic lockfile resolver (pm install/add with SHA-256 seals).

### Track 4: Standard Library Expansion
  [ ] RTB-15: Buffered filesystem stream API (std/fs/file.oo & std/fs/path.oo chunked I/O).
  [ ] RTB-16: Cryptographic hashing & encoding (std/crypto/sha256.oo & std/encoding/base64.oo).
  [ ] RTB-17: Text processing & regular expressions (std/text/regex.oo finite-state engine).

### Track 5: Type System & Formal Verification Depth
  [ ] RTB-18: SMT-backed contract verification (compile-time constraint solving on requires/ensures).
  [ ] RTB-19: Affine & linear typestate lifecycles (compile-time state transitions, no double-free).
  [ ] RTB-20: Zero-cost generics & trait monomorphization (parametric Result[T, E] & List[T] codegen).

### Track 6: Memory Architecture & Hardware-Aware Runtime Depth
  [ ] RTB-21: Scoped arena memory allocators (&ArenaCap high-throughput pointer-bump region reset).
  [ ] RTB-22: Cache-optimized Struct-of-Arrays (SoA / DoD) layout transformation for SIMD vectorization.
